The header comment says `MetadataFacade` implements `IMetadataService`, but the class is not declared as `implements IMetadataService`. Adding the `implements` clause (and importing the type) would make this claim true and prevent accidental interface drift during future changes.
```suggestion
export interface IMetadataService {
  register(type: string, name: string, data: any): Promise<void>;
  get(type: string, name: string): Promise<any>;
  getEntry(type: string, name: string): any;
  list(type: string): Promise<any[]>;
  unregister(type: string, name: string): Promise<void>;
  exists(type: string, name: string): Promise<boolean>;
  listNames(type: string): Promise<string[]>;
  unregisterPackage(packageName: string): Promise<void>;
  getObject(name: string): Promise<any>;
  listObjects(): Promise<any[]>;
}

export class MetadataFacade implements IMetadataService {
```
